WEBVTT

00:00:00.214 --> 00:00:03.888
Meet Gambit: chess you can play and
understand inside Hermes.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.430
On Desktop, make your move on the board.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.527
Hermes calculates a reply, and the live
status shows it working.

00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:19.789
When you need help, ask for a hint.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:22.667
Hermes explains the position in your
existing chat.

00:00:28.243 --> 00:00:31.593
Coach mode connects Stockfish analysis to
your last move,

00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:33.353
with a clear way to improve.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.310
Find your Chess.com or Lichess games by
username.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.361
Choose the exact match to replay.

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:50.514
Make your move in the terminal.

00:00:50.514 --> 00:00:54.239
A live status follows Hermes as it
prepares one reply,

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:55.595
then the board updates.

00:00:59.193 --> 00:01:02.643
Use /chess in CLI or TUI.

00:01:02.643 --> 00:01:06.664
Ask for a clue, then request the next hint
when you want more detail.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.085
In Coach mode, Hermes reviews the move you
just played.

00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:18.435
Stockfish analysis explains what changed
and why it matters.

00:01:18.435 --> 00:01:21.875
Here, pushing the g-pawn exposed the king
to checkmate.

00:01:22.164 --> 00:01:24.514
Play a game. Understand a decision.

00:01:24.609 --> 00:01:27.734
Try another line. Gambit, built for
Hermes.
